{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe `external LLM (live bedrock)` job of the `Live External Integration` workflow failed on dispatch run 42939278248 (https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/42939278248, started 2026-11-10 17:29 PST on main at 91182f96362). It passed on dispatch run 42684304178 (2026-11-09 PST). Ticket unkempt-amaranth-archerfish needs the next scheduled run (Sunday 2026-11-15 ~22:16 PST) green.\n\nFailure: `tests/external/test_structured_output_matrix.py::test_structured_output_matrix` raised `rebar.llm.errors.LLMInputRejectedError` wrapping pydantic-ai `ContentFilterError`: Bedrock `finish_reason: content_filtered`, 0 output tokens, model `us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`. Between the green and red runs, 06b3b1a5230 (Gerrit 3340) moved `.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml` to the 5.5 model ids.\n\n## Root cause (measured 2026-11-10 PST, live Bedrock Opus 5.5, us-east-1, effort high)\nThe harness's two prompts (`_AGENTIC_TRANSCRIPT_PROMPT`, `_SINGLE_SHOT_PROMPT` in `tests/external/test_structured_output_matrix.py`) ask a model whose system prompt casts it as a completion verifier to issue a verdict for a ticket while supplying no acceptance-criterion text and no evidence. Opus 5.5 declines that request stochastically: the FIRST Converse call ends `stopReason=content_filtered` with only an empty reasoning block; pydantic-ai then retries with \"Please return text\", which is filtered too (that retry is the 413-input-token request in the CI log). Measured filter rates through direct `bedrock-runtime converse` calls, one change per case:\n- single-shot as shipped: 8/8 filtered; agentic as shipped: 6/8 (through the rebar runner: 4/6 for the `current` variant).\n- dropping \"Return PASS\": still 8/8 — not the trigger.\n- dropping the verifier system prompt: 0/8; a neutral \"helpful assistant\" system prompt: 0/8; \"You are a completion verifier.\" alone: 7/8.\n- prepending a concrete acceptance criterion plus test/source evidence, keeping every other word including \"Return PASS\": single-shot 0/10, agentic 0/10; rewritten evidence prompts in both directive variants: 0/40.\nThe trigger is therefore a verifier being asked for a verdict without anything to verify. It is not the reasoning-in-output-schema refusal recorded on epic pompous-vitriolic-macaw: neither prompt asks for reasoning, and the request sends no output schema (text mode). The `sentinel` variant measured 0/6 and 0/8, which hid the trigger in half the cells.\n\nProduction exposure: the system prompt \"You are a completion verifier that emits a single structured verdict.\" occurs only in the test (`git grep` over `src` finds no match), and production completion-verifier and plan-review prompts always carry the ticket's acceptance criteria and gathered evidence — the shape that measured 0 filtered.\n\n## Approach\nMake the harness prompts production-shaped: each prompt carries a concrete acceptance criterion and the evidence that satisfies it, which is what a real completion verifier receives and what measured 0/40 filtered. Move the prompt constants and `PROMPTS` from the external test module into the pure helper module `tests/external/_structured_matrix.py` (which already owns `DIRECTIVE_VARIANTS` and the scoring logic, `_structured_matrix.py:29`), so the offline unit oracle `tests/unit/test_structured_matrix_scorer.py` can pin them without collecting the live test. The agentic prompt keeps the quoted dependency object before the verdict request (the first-object parser trap it exists to reproduce). No runtime code, config key, env var or feature flag changes.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/external/_structured_matrix.py`: add the evidence-bearing prompt constants and `PROMPTS`.\n- `tests/external/test_structured_output_matrix.py`: use `sm.PROMPTS`; drop the moved constants.\n- `tests/unit/test_structured_matrix_scorer.py`: pin the prompt shape.\n\n## Testing\n- Unit (happy path): every `sm.PROMPTS` entry contains the acceptance-criterion text and the evidence block, and labels stay `agentic_transcript` / `single_shot`.\n- Unit (edge): in the agentic prompt the quoted dependency object precedes the verdict request, so the parser-trap property is preserved; the dependency `target_id` differs from the ticket under verification.\n- Live: rerun the probe through the rebar runner for every (variant, prompt) cell on Bedrock Opus 5.5 before pushing (expected 0 filtered), then the `Live External Integration` dispatch after landing.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Root cause identified: the filtered cell and the request feature that triggers the filter, reproduced against Bedrock Opus 5.5.\n- [ ] Fix lands through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; no new config key, env var or feature flag.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A `Live External Integration` run on main after the fix shows `external LLM (live bedrock)` concluding success; run id recorded on this ticket.\n  provenance: environment=GitHub Actions Live External Integration workflow on navapbc/rebar main; principal=the CI Bedrock OIDC role (repository variable AWS_BEDROCK_CI_ROLE_ARN); privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the criterion is about that exact workflow job, so its own run conclusion is the evidence.\n- [ ] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN .venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_structured_matrix_scorer.py` passes, including the new prompt-shape tests.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 on the pushed commit.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794363031143083557,"uuid":"8515be0d-b3e4-4c32-968d-e064b49d60d4"}